  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Central Plains Fur Meet (CPFM) was an outdoor camping furmeet at the Lake Afton campground near Wichita, Kansas, started by Merkindesr and Dale Fox. The first meet was held in 2010 at Cheney Lake, and it moved to Lake Afton in 2011. In 2012 the organizers rented an air-conditioned pavilion for dances and a raffle, and in 2013 a spin-off hotel convention, Central Plains Fur Con, was formed. Meets were held through 2014.",
